WEBVTT

00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:25.993
Crew on deck.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.911
How was the delivery to Tokyo?

00:00:28.036 --> 00:00:31.290
Not bad. Mothzilla got into
the ship's closet, though.

00:00:31.623 --> 00:00:34.876
Can we please get
new uniforms now, Professor?

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.170
You said you would replace them
a year ago.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:40.924
You can't expect me to honor
what Year-Ago Professor said.

00:00:41.008 --> 00:00:42.843
That guy was young and foolish.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:47.180
There's nothing wrong with these uniforms
that a few denim patches won't fix.

00:00:51.268 --> 00:00:52.811
Oh, all right.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.813
To the garment district!

00:01:04.031 --> 00:01:05.616
Come in, come in.

00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:09.244
Can I offer you maybe a nice macaroon
cut in seven pieces?

00:01:09.328 --> 00:01:11.538
Such a stereotype.

00:01:11.872 --> 00:01:15.042
Yes, I'm looking for something
in a space uniform

00:01:15.125 --> 00:01:17.461
that's respectfully humiliating

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:20.756
but can come out of an employee's salary
without his noticing.

00:01:21.131 --> 00:01:24.426
You got it.
Tomorrow's clothes at yesterday's prices.

00:01:25.844 --> 00:01:28.847
Ah. You can't go wrong with a still suit.

00:01:28.931 --> 00:01:32.351
It recycles your solid waste
into a nice piece gefilte fish.

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:33.560
Ugh.

00:01:33.644 --> 00:01:36.104
Is there a way to just keep it
as solid waste?

00:01:38.106 --> 00:01:40.692
Now here's
something we can all agree on.

00:01:42.736 --> 00:01:45.280
The Stardoz 2293.

00:01:45.364 --> 00:01:47.824
Not for everybody, but you pull it off.

00:01:47.908 --> 00:01:49.284
Please don't pull it off.

00:01:49.618 --> 00:01:53.747
Yo, Squidward Scissorhands,
you got this in an adult robot medium?

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.457
The foxhunting uniform?

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:58.335
You, sir, must be a robot
of noble bearings.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:01.463
Well, I am descended
from Prince Albert's can.

00:02:01.838 --> 00:02:04.049
I think we've seen enough.

00:02:04.132 --> 00:02:07.386
Too much, actually.
Come on, let's try somewhere else.

00:02:07.636 --> 00:02:10.889
Wait, wait, perhaps
discerning customers like yourselves

00:02:10.973 --> 00:02:13.475
would be interested in an item
from our discount rack.

00:02:13.809 --> 00:02:16.061
Quality is the most important thing.

00:02:16.144 --> 00:02:17.271
How much is it?

00:02:17.563 --> 00:02:19.064
90% off.

00:02:19.147 --> 00:02:22.401
An unpleasant fellow
ordered them last year but never paid.

00:02:22.484 --> 00:02:23.902
Most unpleasant, that one.

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:27.656
That sounds like something
Year-Ago Professor would do.

00:02:27.739 --> 00:02:28.782
We'll take them.

00:02:36.206 --> 00:02:39.585
Finally, a uniform I'd be happy
to be caught dead in.

00:02:39.668 --> 00:02:43.714
And, boy, does it wick away moisture,
gallons and gallons of it.

00:02:43.922 --> 00:02:45.507
Plus, they're stitched in such a way

00:02:45.591 --> 00:02:47.676
that, no matter what angle
it's viewed from,

00:02:47.759 --> 00:02:49.970
it looks like
you're standing in hero wind.

00:02:50.345 --> 00:02:53.015
I just wish my fists
weren't sewn to my belt.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.811
Hey, what's Bender wearing
instead of that crap?

00:02:57.895 --> 00:03:00.689
Oh, Lord. Did you actually buy that getup?

00:03:00.856 --> 00:03:04.276
We foxhunters do not stoop to buy getups.

00:03:04.359 --> 00:03:05.944
I made free with it.

00:03:06.028 --> 00:03:09.489
Since when do you care
or even know about foxhunting?

00:03:09.698 --> 00:03:12.117
Foxhunting is an ancient and noble pursuit

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.787
that's fascinated me ever since
I first heard of it 10 minutes ago.

00:03:15.954 --> 00:03:20.125
Noble pursuit? What's noble
about killing a defenseless animal?

00:03:20.208 --> 00:03:24.338
Don't be naive, Leela.
We kill defenseless animals all the time.

00:03:24.421 --> 00:03:26.715
Look at Hermes's tortoiseshell glasses.

00:03:26.798 --> 00:03:29.384
The Professor's walrus-ivory teeth.

00:03:29.468 --> 00:03:31.845
And don't forget the zebra-fur ship cozy.

00:03:31.929 --> 00:03:33.305
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:03:33.388 --> 00:03:34.514
He's got a point.

00:03:34.848 --> 00:03:37.935
See, Leela, there are two sides
to every shameful act.

00:03:38.018 --> 00:03:42.314
What you call the atrocity of crazed dogs
tearing a helpless fox to shreds,

00:03:42.397 --> 00:03:44.524
others call a pleasant jaunt in the park.

00:03:44.608 --> 00:03:45.692
The first thing.

00:03:45.776 --> 00:03:46.902
Come see for yourself.

00:03:47.152 --> 00:03:50.572
Join me on the morrow
as I embark on my maiden hunt.

00:03:51.114 --> 00:03:52.282
I said join me!

00:04:01.758 --> 00:04:03.844
This is my best protest sign ever,

00:04:04.094 --> 00:04:08.223
and it was easy because I started
with a "save the ox" sign I already had.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:12.311
Wow, where'd you get the horse?

00:04:12.519 --> 00:04:14.146
None of your business.

00:04:24.406 --> 00:04:28.952
Young man, one does not drink from
a champagne fountain in that manner.

00:04:29.328 --> 00:04:30.829
But he's doing it.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.710
Check out this dork.

00:04:37.002 --> 00:04:39.630
I, sir, am the master of the hunt,

00:04:39.713 --> 00:04:42.174
and I'll thank you
to behave like a gentleman.

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.217
You're quite welcome, sir.

00:04:49.765 --> 00:04:51.642
Ah, yes, foxhunting.

00:04:51.725 --> 00:04:54.561
If there's one thing I know,
it's everything about it.

00:04:55.979 --> 00:04:57.105
What's that weird cat?

00:04:58.357 --> 00:05:01.234
This is the fox we'll be hunting today.

00:05:01.485 --> 00:05:03.445
Wow, this is easier than I thought.

00:05:03.528 --> 00:05:05.614
The sport is in the chase, sir.

00:05:05.781 --> 00:05:08.575
The fox gets a 30-minute head start.

00:05:14.206 --> 00:05:17.209
Man, it would have been so much easier
to kill it in the cage.

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.676
Let the hunt begin.

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:36.186
Stop, this is cruel and inhumane.

00:05:36.687 --> 00:05:39.856
Well, now, in all my years
as a hunt master,

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.650
I've never seen anything like this.

00:05:41.984 --> 00:05:44.987
I mean, look at that sign.
It's magnificent.

00:05:45.362 --> 00:05:47.489
Oh! Thank you.

00:05:47.572 --> 00:05:51.118
I used a ruler and I erased
all the pencil lines when I was finished.

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:53.829
Charming. Now, into the ditch with you.

00:06:01.503 --> 00:06:06.091
So the dogs do all the work while
we sportsmen enjoy a nice horsey ride?

00:06:06.174 --> 00:06:09.094
Precisely. I see you've caught the fever.

00:06:09.177 --> 00:06:10.470
Keep your wits about you.

00:06:10.554 --> 00:06:13.015
I've blanketed these woods
with devious traps

00:06:13.098 --> 00:06:15.392
to ward off poachers and protesters.

00:06:16.351 --> 00:06:18.562
Stop the bloodshed, stop the violence.

00:06:19.313 --> 00:06:20.397
Ha!

00:06:20.981 --> 00:06:24.484
I saw that coming
from a mile...

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:29.990
Be more careful, friend.

00:06:30.073 --> 00:06:33.577
My antigravity snares
are virtually undetectable.

00:06:34.786 --> 00:06:37.539
I saw it coming from a mile...

00:06:39.291 --> 00:06:41.293
View halloo, view halloo.

00:06:41.376 --> 00:06:44.046
View halloo? All right.
What does that mean?

00:06:44.338 --> 00:06:45.839
The fox has been sighted.

00:06:50.969 --> 00:06:53.930
Yeah, get that fox. Go, dogs, go.

00:07:01.688 --> 00:07:02.773
Either way.

00:07:13.241 --> 00:07:15.953
Oh, God, this is horrible. I can't watch.

00:07:16.286 --> 00:07:19.289
Pfft. You humans always say
you don't want to see violence,

00:07:19.373 --> 00:07:20.540
but you know you do.

00:07:20.624 --> 00:07:22.292
I defy you not to watch.

00:07:30.008 --> 00:07:32.386
A robot fox? Huh.

00:07:32.844 --> 00:07:35.222
I guess I'm okay with this after all.

00:07:35.847 --> 00:07:37.224
Well, I'm not.

00:07:37.307 --> 00:07:40.143
Robot foxhunting is a
crime against robo-nature.

00:07:40.644 --> 00:07:43.814
Stop the bloodshed, stop the...

00:07:49.528 --> 00:07:52.990
How can you do this
to a poor, defenseless robot animal?

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.410
You people are sick,
and you foxhounds are no better.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:08:00.414
They're not foxhounds.
They're springer spaniels, you twit.

00:08:02.499 --> 00:08:04.918
Or rather spring-powered spaniels.

00:08:06.169 --> 00:08:08.880
Bot-on-bot violence? Where will it end?

00:08:09.172 --> 00:08:11.675
Not with the dogs. Come here, Sea Gasket.

00:08:21.685 --> 00:08:27.816
No! You, sir, are a heartless monster,
and you will rue the day you met me.

00:08:28.066 --> 00:08:30.694
Also, can I get my parking validated?

00:08:36.074 --> 00:08:39.911
The time has come to end
injustice against robot animals.

00:08:42.164 --> 00:08:45.626
No dog track rabbit
should be used to test cosmetics,

00:08:45.709 --> 00:08:48.920
no robot cow should have to be
milked by a milking machine,

00:08:49.087 --> 00:08:52.174
and no milking machine
should have to milk a robot cow.

00:08:52.466 --> 00:08:54.676
Those injustices don't even exist.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.471
Then let's find some that do.

00:09:04.311 --> 00:09:09.066
Robot chickens weren't made to be
jammed in cubicles and forced to lay eggs.

00:09:09.149 --> 00:09:10.776
Actually, they was.

00:09:14.988 --> 00:09:16.365
I'll save you.

00:09:16.907 --> 00:09:19.159
Run free, sweet robo-hen.

00:09:29.878 --> 00:09:33.340
Enough with the tenderizing.
It's time for a Benderizing.

00:09:34.758 --> 00:09:37.678
Hey, you people can't just burst in
like that and cut off my hand.

00:09:37.761 --> 00:09:38.845
You got to take a number.

00:09:49.398 --> 00:09:52.359
Shooting innocent robot ducks is wrong.

00:09:53.485 --> 00:09:55.946
Fly away. Fly away, my pretties.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.535
You did it!

00:10:01.618 --> 00:10:02.828
Congratulations, Bender,

00:10:02.995 --> 00:10:07.374
you've ended robot animal cruelty
within a 20-yard radius of this building.

00:10:07.457 --> 00:10:11.336
You ready to call it a day,
or do you have one more score to settle?

00:10:11.753 --> 00:10:13.588
The second thing.

00:10:15.549 --> 00:10:18.093
The weekly hunt is hereby called to order.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.430
I'll drink some more to that.

00:10:21.763 --> 00:10:26.476
As always, once I release the fox, it will
have a 30-minute head start before...

00:10:28.103 --> 00:10:29.187
Stop the hunt.

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:34.192
- You again.
- I'm back, snooty.

00:10:35.277 --> 00:10:39.364
We're here to liberate that robot fox,
and that's what we're gonna do.

00:10:42.618 --> 00:10:44.119
Do you mind showing me
how to open the cage?

00:10:44.369 --> 00:10:47.456
Now, listen here,
the hunt is a hallowed tradition,

00:10:47.623 --> 00:10:50.917
and you Bambi-loving beatniks
will never stop it.

00:10:51.001 --> 00:10:52.836
Oh, no? Well, for your information,

00:10:52.919 --> 00:10:56.381
the robot fox has been declared
an endangered robo-species.

00:10:56.882 --> 00:11:00.594
This injunction suspends all robot
foxhunting for 24 hours

00:11:00.677 --> 00:11:02.638
while our motion is under consideration.

00:11:03.305 --> 00:11:05.432
We'll see you in court.

00:11:12.147 --> 00:11:16.151
Motion destroyed.
The hunt shall resume at sunup.

00:11:19.988 --> 00:11:21.698
He's crooked, but fair.

00:11:24.743 --> 00:11:26.119
I'm not giving up yet.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.038
- I am.
- I already did.

00:11:28.121 --> 00:11:30.749
You can count on me.
Now, here's the plan.

00:11:30.832 --> 00:11:33.543
We're going to sneak onto the grounds
and free that fox.

00:11:33.627 --> 00:11:35.712
Can we stop for ice cream
on the way back?

00:11:35.796 --> 00:11:37.172
All right, fine.

00:11:37.506 --> 00:11:39.132
And on the way there?

00:11:42.094 --> 00:11:45.013
Okay, I'll hold the ice cream
while you two go over.

00:11:50.894 --> 00:11:51.979
Where's the ice cream?

00:11:52.479 --> 00:11:53.939
There was a bear.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.864
Okay. You guys take him back
to Planet Express.

00:12:03.323 --> 00:12:06.034
I've got one more shenanigan
up my sleeve.

00:12:06.451 --> 00:12:08.662
But you promised us way-back ice cream.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.082
Here. But no chocolate, it's bedtime.

00:12:16.044 --> 00:12:18.463
With that odious robot
barred from the grounds,

00:12:18.547 --> 00:12:21.758
the weekly hunt is hereby called
once more to order.

00:12:22.134 --> 00:12:23.677
Let the hunt begin.

00:12:26.763 --> 00:12:29.391
You, sir, have been outfoxed.

00:12:30.934 --> 00:12:32.394
I spent all night on that.

00:12:32.561 --> 00:12:36.273
It's clever.
Nevertheless, I demand you return my fox.

00:12:36.565 --> 00:12:39.735
Sorry, mutton-chump. No fox, no hunt.

00:12:40.027 --> 00:12:41.653
Oh, really?

00:12:45.616 --> 00:12:46.908
Let the hunt begin!

00:12:51.913 --> 00:12:55.417
Sir, I leave you with
this one final thought.

00:13:03.467 --> 00:13:08.138
Oh, God, they're gonna kill me,
el roboto más importante.

00:13:08.221 --> 00:13:10.098
And I only have a 30-minute head start.

00:13:10.557 --> 00:13:12.768
Uh-oh, a fork in the path.

00:13:14.186 --> 00:13:16.688
There's more places to hide
in that dark forest.

00:13:16.772 --> 00:13:19.399
On the other hand, I could run faster
through that open meadow.

00:13:19.858 --> 00:13:23.946
But of course, the forest might protect
my fair robot skin from sunburn.

00:13:24.446 --> 00:13:26.156
Hmm...

00:13:33.747 --> 00:13:38.543
Today, we hunt the most dangerous game,
aside from lawn darts,

00:13:38.627 --> 00:13:42.673
a cunning robotic adversary
so deviously clever that...

00:13:43.215 --> 00:13:45.258
For God's sake.

00:13:45.342 --> 00:13:48.887
Then again, a nice run through a meadow,
who could say no to that?

00:13:48.971 --> 00:13:50.097
What?

00:13:52.474 --> 00:13:56.728
Look here. Hunting is a team effort,
and you're not pulling your weight.

00:13:56.812 --> 00:14:00.524
Now, I'm going to be sporting
and give you one more chance to run.

00:14:00.941 --> 00:14:04.695
Thanks. Nothing's more important
than sportsmanship.

00:14:09.741 --> 00:14:12.619
It's so cute. Horseshoe crab cute.

00:14:18.583 --> 00:14:20.460
Fox news, everyone.

00:14:20.544 --> 00:14:24.423
I've decided to make the fox
our new corporate mascot.

00:14:24.631 --> 00:14:29.970
Hear, hear. Let's put on our new uniforms
and take a staff photo for the newsletter.

00:14:30.053 --> 00:14:31.138
Right on!

00:14:31.763 --> 00:14:34.516
Here they are, freshly laundered and...

00:14:39.187 --> 00:14:42.983
Our magnificent uniforms. They're ruined.

00:14:44.776 --> 00:14:48.405
And he peed on the locker room floor.
That's my territory.

00:14:49.156 --> 00:14:52.909
Also got in the henhouse and killed
Amy's prize-winning Rhode Island Red.

00:14:53.076 --> 00:14:54.745
Not Penelope.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:58.165
Cute or not, I'll kill that robo-rat.

00:15:02.919 --> 00:15:04.046
Let me at it.

00:15:04.129 --> 00:15:06.548
I'm gonna pound it
with this chewed-up old stick.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:10.010
No! It's just a poor, scared wild robot.

00:15:10.093 --> 00:15:12.137
What did you expect?

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.181
My sign. It's ruined.

00:15:14.848 --> 00:15:15.932
Kill the fox.

00:15:32.532 --> 00:15:34.910
Missed it by that much.

00:15:39.164 --> 00:15:41.083
Oh, no, they caught my scent.

00:15:41.166 --> 00:15:43.543
I better throw them off
by rubbing myself with something.

00:15:47.005 --> 00:15:49.091
That's no good.

00:15:49.174 --> 00:15:52.260
Wait, I know what'll confuse those dogs.
Catnip.

00:16:04.606 --> 00:16:06.900
You have made yourself
an enemy, my friend!

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:18.370
Dang it. He jumped on
the PATH train to New Jersey.

00:16:18.453 --> 00:16:21.748
Of course. He's commuting
back to his native habitat.

00:16:30.966 --> 00:16:33.135
On top of everything, I'm starving.

00:16:33.218 --> 00:16:35.512
I'll have to carve a sandwich
out of this tree branch.

00:16:39.349 --> 00:16:40.392
Ow!

00:16:40.475 --> 00:16:44.521
My finger. I wish I remembered
more survival skills from Boy Scouts.

00:16:44.855 --> 00:16:47.608
Too bad my only merit badge
was in interpretive dance.

00:16:48.358 --> 00:16:52.154
Wait. I can use the universal language
of dance to signal for help.

00:16:56.366 --> 00:16:57.451
Ow!

00:16:57.534 --> 00:17:00.162
That was my second-favorite ankle.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.751
Was that a horn? Are those the dogs?

00:17:06.835 --> 00:17:09.463
Is that two caterpillars
making sweet love?

00:17:10.881 --> 00:17:11.965
Aw...

00:17:12.049 --> 00:17:14.551
You know what it's like
to feel hunted, too, buddy?

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.013
Would it be too much to ask you
to stay with me in my final moments

00:17:18.096 --> 00:17:19.931
and die at my side?

00:17:20.015 --> 00:17:21.308
And you die first?

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.062
You lousy son of a...

00:17:25.896 --> 00:17:28.023
I get it. You freed me.

00:17:29.566 --> 00:17:31.234
You lousy son of a...

00:17:38.575 --> 00:17:40.327
We're hot on his heels.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.453
A-ha!

00:17:41.536 --> 00:17:42.913
One of his heels.

00:17:48.085 --> 00:17:50.087
Oh... These guys.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.588
Can I help you?

00:17:51.672 --> 00:17:54.049
Out of our way. This fox is ours.

00:17:54.132 --> 00:17:57.260
Fox? Yes. Have at it.

00:17:57.344 --> 00:17:59.471
We're not hunting fox today.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:02.641
Wait a second. What are you hunting?

00:18:03.642 --> 00:18:06.561
Oh, my God. It's Bender's middle finger.

00:18:06.645 --> 00:18:08.647
I'd recognize this anywhere.

00:18:16.321 --> 00:18:20.450
What is it, little buddy? Is it a
layer cake? Or maybe World Series tickets?

00:18:22.619 --> 00:18:26.623
A trip wire. But who's tripping who?

00:18:32.546 --> 00:18:35.299
Wait, whom. Who's tripping whom?

00:18:39.261 --> 00:18:42.556
I guess what I've been trying to say is
we should all be ashamed.

00:18:42.973 --> 00:18:46.602
Me for my hatred of a mechanical fox
that tore up my sign

00:18:46.685 --> 00:18:48.312
and who I'd like to throttle,

00:18:48.562 --> 00:18:51.273
and you for hunting an innocent robot.

00:18:51.857 --> 00:18:54.568
Well, a robot who didn't
harm you personally.

00:18:55.068 --> 00:18:56.945
Today. Probably.

00:18:57.696 --> 00:19:00.657
But most of all, I blame you, hunt master.

00:19:02.576 --> 00:19:03.660
Where's the hunt master?

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:07.831
Remember when you said "nobody leave"
and then you turned your head briefly?

00:19:07.914 --> 00:19:09.374
He left an hour before that.

00:19:32.522 --> 00:19:34.483
You disappoint me, Bender.

00:19:34.566 --> 00:19:38.779
I'd have thought you'd have learned
to avoid my antigravity snares by now.

00:19:38.862 --> 00:19:41.156
I did. Too bad you didn't.

00:19:43.575 --> 00:19:44.660
Ye gods!

00:19:49.998 --> 00:19:51.959
How does it feel to be the hunted?

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:54.086
To be forever looking over your shoulder,

00:19:54.461 --> 00:19:56.213
like an owl with that type of neck?

00:19:56.755 --> 00:20:00.592
To die in agony at the hands
of the world's greatest lover?

00:20:01.551 --> 00:20:02.928
No! Please!

00:20:06.431 --> 00:20:07.891
I can't shoot you.

00:20:09.142 --> 00:20:11.103
Bender, I found your trigger finger.

00:20:11.186 --> 00:20:12.479
Now I can.

00:20:13.897 --> 00:20:16.692
But I won't. Not with so many witnesses.

00:20:16.942 --> 00:20:18.819
You're a true gentleman.

00:20:18.902 --> 00:20:20.070
Unlike me.

00:20:28.829 --> 00:20:30.497
I can't watch...

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:31.665
Enough.

00:20:32.916 --> 00:20:34.001
Oh, no!

00:20:36.128 --> 00:20:37.421
Hey, wait a minute.

00:20:40.882 --> 00:20:43.260
He was also a robot? Dude!

00:20:43.635 --> 00:20:46.096
So a robot fox killed a robot human?

00:20:46.471 --> 00:20:48.348
I guess that makes it okay.

00:20:48.432 --> 00:20:50.851
No. Killing of any kind is...

00:20:51.268 --> 00:20:52.936
I don't know, well...

00:20:53.437 --> 00:20:54.813
Let me think about this.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:04.906
I guess it's okay.